you know, traditional in group.

1310
00:53:11.910 --> 00:53:12.900
Yeah.

1311
00:53:12.900 --> 00:53:15.150
Yes, and something that you hear a lot

1312
00:53:15.150 --> 00:53:17.820
when you talk to people who work in deradicalization,

1313
00:53:17.820 --> 00:53:20.370
whether it's online or not online,

1314
00:53:20.370 --> 00:53:23.370
is that often the answer, even though it sounds pat,

1315
00:53:23.370 --> 00:53:24.480
it sounds simplistic,

1316
00:53:24.480 --> 00:53:25.950
is just to help someone find

1317
00:53:25.950 --> 00:53:27.840
a new sense of community and connection.

1318
00:53:27.840 --> 00:53:30.870
And a lot of the stories end with,

1319
00:53:30.870 --> 00:53:33.000
you know, oh, he was in an extremist group,

1320
00:53:33.000 --> 00:53:34.230
but then he got a girlfriend

1321
00:53:34.230 --> 00:53:39.230
And it sounds like like it couldn't possibly be that simple

1322
00:53:39.300 --> 00:53:41.700
or it couldn't possibly be that superficial.

1323
00:53:41.700 --> 00:53:42.870
And it does, when it's weighed up

1324
00:53:42.870 --> 00:53:44.550
against a great political cause,

1325
00:53:44.550 --> 00:53:46.710
you say, well, how could you deradicalize someone

1326
00:53:46.710 --> 00:53:51.360
from believing in, you know, literal race genocide

1327
00:53:51.360 --> 00:53:53.610
by getting a partner, getting a romantic partner.

1328
00:53:53.610 --> 00:53:55.950
But the need that is driving it

1329
00:53:55.950 --> 00:53:57.750
is ultimately rarely political.

1330
00:53:57.750 --> 00:54:00.060
And it is usually personal and that sense of connection.

1331
00:54:00.060 --> 00:54:02.760
Someone finding a church,

1332
00:54:02.760 --> 00:54:04.110
or finding another sense of community.

1333
00:54:04.110 --> 00:54:07.440
I mean the thing that I did to kind of unplug myself

1334
00:54:07.440 --> 00:54:11.520
from social media and to, you know,

1335
00:54:11.520 --> 00:54:12.690
I don't think I was radicalized,

1336
00:54:12.690 --> 00:54:14.557
but we're all micro-radicalized by social media.

1337
00:54:14.557 --> 00:54:18.120
The thing that I did to de-micro-radicalize myself

1338
00:54:18.120 --> 00:54:22.740
was just find group chats,

1339
00:54:22.740 --> 00:54:25.440
and just set up a like Slack of friend groups

1340
00:54:25.440 --> 00:54:27.180
that I've used to replace social media

1341
00:54:27.180 --> 00:54:29.970
and just spend more time with people in person,

1342
00:54:29.970 --> 00:54:31.560
which it sounds so pat,

1343
00:54:31.560 --> 00:54:33.870
it sounds like they couldn't possibly be the answer,

1344
00:54:33.870 --> 00:54:34.950
but I think it really is.

1345
00:54:34.950 --> 00:54:38.460
Yeah, so you changed your media--

1346
00:54:38.460 --> 00:54:39.293
Exactly.

1347
00:54:39.293 --> 00:54:40.380
Diet habits.

1348
00:54:40.380 --> 00:54:41.213
Right.

1349
00:54:41.213 --> 00:54:42.540
So what changes did you make?

1350
00:54:42.540 --> 00:54:45.120
So the answer that you usually will hear people say,

1351
00:54:45.120 --> 00:54:48.330
I was just listening to an interview with someone

1352
00:54:48.330 --> 00:54:49.230
who was talking about this.

1353
00:54:49.230 --> 00:54:52.680
And she was saying, well, spend some time on social media

1354
00:54:52.680 --> 00:54:55.590
and then spend some time reading traditional news outlets

1355
00:54:55.590 --> 00:54:57.030
and try to determine which one

1356
00:54:57.030 --> 00:54:58.380
is giving you better information.

1357
00:54:58.380 --> 00:55:01.230
And that made me laugh because we know the answer,

1358
00:55:01.230 --> 00:55:03.660
and also that's not how people work.

1359
00:55:03.660 --> 00:55:06.300
You know, that's not why people are spending more time

1360
00:55:06.300 --> 00:55:07.133
on social media.

1361
00:55:07.133 --> 00:55:09.537
I think the replacement that I made

1362
00:55:09.537 --> 00:55:11.430
and that I would really encourage people to make

1363
00:55:11.430 --> 00:55:13.053
is to identify the thing that social media is giving

1364
00:55:13.053 --> 00:55:17.340
that you're finding addictive is the feeling of validation,

1365
00:55:17.340 --> 00:55:18.267
the feeling of connection,

1366
00:55:18.267 --> 00:55:21.210
the feeling of having a community who support,

1367
00:55:21.210 --> 00:55:22.410
maybe you're getting or not getting,

1368
00:55:22.410 --> 00:55:24.060
but you are definitely chasing.

1369
00:55:24.060 --> 00:55:25.983
And if you can replace that with,

1370
00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:28.200
you know, a group of runners,

1371
00:55:28.200 --> 00:55:29.760
or a group that you go cycling with,

1372
00:55:29.760 --> 00:55:33.750
or what I did, and just had a big like group chat

1373
00:55:33.750 --> 00:55:35.760
that I check in with 30 times a day

1374
00:55:35.760 --> 00:55:38.160
instead of checking Facebook and Twitter 30 times a day,

1375
00:55:38.160 --> 00:55:41.090
it will supplant the need that is driving you

1376
00:55:41.090 --> 00:55:42.480
to the social platforms.

1377
00:55:42.480 --> 00:55:43.620
And I think that will take care

1378
00:55:43.620 --> 00:55:45.330
of a lot of the downstream effects

1379
00:55:45.330 --> 00:55:46.163
of how it's changing your politics,

1380
00:55:46.163 --> 00:55:48.090
how it's changing our emotional balance.

1381
00:55:48.090 --> 00:55:52.440
Yeah, so there's that piece, that feeling of connection

1382
00:55:52.440 --> 00:55:54.480
and the external validation

1383
00:55:54.480 --> 00:55:56.400
that comes with social media use,

1384
00:55:56.400 --> 00:55:59.400
but sort of related, but separate

1385
00:55:59.400 --> 00:56:04.400
is the issue of validating your information feed, right?

1386
00:56:04.710 --> 00:56:05.781
Sure.

1387
00:56:05.781 --> 00:56:07.680
There's misinformation, there's disinformation,

1388
00:56:07.680 --> 00:56:11.820
there's propaganda, there's traditional news sources,

1389
00:56:11.820 --> 00:56:16.380
and more and more, people are consuming their news online.

1390
00:56:16.380 --> 00:56:18.180
They're not going offline

1391
00:56:18.180 --> 00:56:20.820
to actually get a physical newspaper,

1392
00:56:20.820 --> 00:56:24.030
or less and less are they watching cable news.

1393
00:56:24.030 --> 00:56:27.120
It's more about like what shows up in their feed, right?

1394
00:56:27.120 --> 00:56:30.900
And these new, you know, quote unquote, news sources,

1395
00:56:30.900 --> 00:56:33.960
some of some legit and some of ill repute,

1396
00:56:33.960 --> 00:56:35.190
it's becoming more and more,

1397
00:56:35.190 --> 00:56:37.860
you have to become a lot more savvy and sophisticated

1398
00:56:37.860 --> 00:56:39.480
to discern the difference

1399
00:56:39.480 --> 00:56:41.820
between what is vetted and legitimate

1400
00:56:41.820 --> 00:56:44.940
versus something that is not, right?

1401
00:56:44.940 --> 00:56:48.750
And I don't see that problem getting any easier to solve.

1402
00:56:48.750 --> 00:56:51.120
I mean, I think, you know, especially young users

1403
00:56:51.120 --> 00:56:54.660
are more sophisticated in certain ways of under,

1404
00:56:54.660 --> 00:56:57.510
you know, they're more internet literate,

1405
00:56:57.510 --> 00:57:01.050
but I don't, I see this problem becoming more problematic,

1406
00:57:01.050 --> 00:57:04.320
especially as technology advances,

1407
00:57:04.320 --> 00:57:06.540
and, you know, we're gonna see deep fakes,

1408
00:57:06.540 --> 00:57:09.180
and all this other kind of, it's gonna get super crazy

1409
00:57:09.180 --> 00:57:11.880
compared to what it it's gonna feel quaint right now

1410
00:57:11.880 --> 00:57:13.950
compared to where it's headed.

1411
00:57:13.950 --> 00:57:15.540
And I don't see a lot of discussion

1412
00:57:15.540 --> 00:57:17.700
about how we're gonna manage that,

1413
00:57:17.700 --> 00:57:21.480
or what we're doing right now to kind of vet news sources.

1414
00:57:21.480 --> 00:57:23.427
Right, so this is, I think,

1415
00:57:23.427 --> 00:57:28.427
one of my most kind of categorical takes on social media

1416
00:57:28.440 --> 00:57:30.450
and how to deal with it is that you are, I think,

1417
00:57:30.450 --> 00:57:32.370
full stop, not going to be accurately informed

1418
00:57:32.370 --> 00:57:33.570
on social media.

1419
00:57:33.570 --> 00:57:36.750
And it's not just, are you following the right accounts?

1420
00:57:36.750 --> 00:57:39.270
Are you, you know, careful about which news sources you read

1421
00:57:39.270 --> 00:57:40.710
because you could do that,

1422
00:57:40.710 --> 00:57:43.920
but the ways that things are framed on social media

1423
00:57:43.920 --> 00:57:46.830
is still going to be consistently misleading.

1424
00:57:46.830 --> 00:57:48.330
And it's more fundamental than that too.

1425
00:57:48.330 --> 00:57:51.390
The way that you consume information

1426
00:57:51.390 --> 00:57:55.230
completely flips and changes when it's in a social context

1427
00:57:55.230 --> 00:57:56.730
than when you're just reading an article.

1428
00:57:56.730 --> 00:57:58.860
There's this really fascinating study

1429
00:57:58.860 --> 00:58:00.270
that I write about in the book,

1430
00:58:00.270 --> 00:58:01.800
where a bunch of researchers

1431
00:58:01.800 --> 00:58:04.950
got some Republicans, Conservative voters,

1432
00:58:04.950 --> 00:58:07.440
and they showed them a, what was it?

1433
00:58:07.440 --> 00:58:11.610
It was a fake headline about Central American refugees

1434
00:58:11.610 --> 00:58:12.443
showing up at the border.

1435
00:58:12.443 --> 00:58:13.860
It said something outrageous,

1436
00:58:13.860 --> 00:58:17.190
like all the refugees are actually criminals with ISIS,

1437
00:58:17.190 --> 00:58:19.380
something clearly false.

1438
00:58:19.380 --> 00:58:21.120
And if they would ask people,

1439
00:58:21.120 --> 00:58:24.480
even very serious committed Republicans,

1440
00:58:24.480 --> 00:58:27.000
whether or not they considered the headline to be true,

1441
00:58:27.000 --> 00:58:28.230
just the headline, do you think it's true?

1442
00:58:28.230 --> 00:58:30.810
The overall majority would say, no, that's not true.

1443
00:58:30.810 --> 00:58:31.877
And then they would ask them,

1444
00:58:31.877 --> 00:58:34.140
do you wanna share that on Facebook?

1445
00:58:34.140 --> 00:58:35.790
And they would say, no, I don't wanna share it on Facebook

1446
00:58:35.790 --> 00:58:37.590
because it's not true.

1447
00:58:37.590 --> 00:58:40.440
But if they showed another set

1448
00:58:40.440 --> 00:58:43.590
of Republicans Conservatives the same headline,

1449
00:58:43.590 --> 00:58:45.660
but they dressed it up as a Facebook post,

1450
00:58:45.660 --> 00:58:47.520
and if the first question they asked was,

1451
00:58:47.520 --> 00:58:48.840
do you wanna share that on Facebook?

1452
00:58:48.840 --> 00:58:51.150
The overwhelming majority would say yes.

1453
00:58:51.150 --> 00:58:52.590
And then if they asked, is that true?

1454
00:58:52.590 --> 00:58:53.700
They would say, yes, that's true

1455
00:58:53.700 --> 00:58:55.560
because I just shared it on Facebook.

1456
00:58:55.560 --> 00:58:58.680
So when we are in a social context,

1457
00:58:58.680 --> 00:59:00.150
we're not judging for accuracy.

1458
00:59:00.150 --> 00:59:02.280
We might think we are, we might be trying to,

1459
00:59:02.280 --> 00:59:05.460
we might have set up the right outlets to follow,

1460
00:59:05.460 --> 00:59:06.480
but it's not where we're looking for.

1461
00:59:06.480 --> 00:59:09.210
We're looking for is identity, we're looking for validation,

1462
00:59:09.210 --> 00:59:11.970
we're looking for things that we think

1463
00:59:11.970 --> 00:59:14.520
other people in our community wanna see.

1464
00:59:14.520 --> 00:59:17.730
So I think my advice for individuals,

1465
00:59:17.730 --> 00:59:20.040
which doesn't solve the problem systemically, I know,

1466
00:59:20.040 --> 00:59:23.520
is just don't read headlines or news in a social context.

1467
00:59:23.520 --> 00:59:24.353
Just don't do it.

1468
00:59:24.353 --> 00:59:25.186
Good luck with that.

1469
00:59:25.186 --> 00:59:26.277
I know, you know?

1470
00:59:27.360 --> 00:59:28.770
Sorry to interrupt the flow.

1471
